      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "On turn 1, with Sarkhan (a 2-drop requiring {1}{R}) in hand and Sacred Foundry available, playing a basic Mountain instead of Sacred Foundry is slightly suboptimal. Sacred Foundry on turn 1 (paying 2 life to have it enter untapped) and a basic Mountain on turn 2 would yield the same mana for casting Sarkhan on turn 2. However, playing Sacred Foundry turn 1 preserves more flexibility: if the player draws a white or Plains-matters card, they already have the dual land in play. More importantly, Maelstrom of the Spirit Dragon could be played on turn 2 instead of a basic Mountain, giving access to Dragon-colored mana and the Dragon tutor ability later. Playing Mountain first slightly reduces sequencing flexibility, though the practical impact is small since Sarkhan only needs {1}{R}.",
      "action_taken": "Played a basic Mountain on turn 1.",
      "better_line": "Play Sacred Foundry (paying 2 life) on turn 1 to maximize flexibility, keeping open the option to play Maelstrom of the Spirit Dragon on turn 2 while still curving into Sarkhan.",
